**Security decisions implemented:**
- All S3 operations execute server-side only; no AWS credentials reach the client
- Server-side authentication via NextAuth session; user ID never accepted from client
- File type validation against allowlist; size limits enforced
- Filename sanitization prevents path traversal and XSS
- User isolation via UUID-based file keys with user ID prefix
- Ownership verification before file deletion (404 for non-owned files)
- Rate limiting on upload endpoint
- Structured error logging without sensitive data
- Minimal response data returned to client
